{"uncertainty": 0.3, "outcome": "Submitted axil_timer.v (rtl_source) and axil_timer_tb.v (testbench). The platform still has to run lint, simulation and synthesis over them. No formal_spec file is submitted.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "design_decision", "title": "Implementation choices traced to the approved specs", "summary": "The channel logic follows section 1 of [artifact:prj-97dea43f5b.microarchitecture.a1]. aw_held and w_held hold a write address or data that arrives alone, with awready = !aw_held && !bvalid, wready = !w_held && !bvalid and arready = !rvalid. The timer next-state is one combinational block with defaults and overrides in the specified order: count step, then the expiry clear, then the expiry set, then the CTRL write, then the LOAD byte merge. The register block only applies reset or q <= d. Address decode uses addr[1:0]==0 and (addr>>4)==0, so offsets from 0x10 up never alias a register at ADDR_WIDTH 8, as section 6 of [artifact:prj-97dea43f5b.interface-spec.a1] requires. All of this serves [requirement:req-2b2b91a584]."}, {"kind": "open_item", "title": "Formal proof not delivered in this submission", "summary": "Section 8 of [artifact:prj-97dea43f5b.interface-spec.a1] and the plan in [artifact:prj-97dea43f5b.microarchitecture.a1] ask for SymbiYosys proofs at ADDR_WIDTH 4 and 8. This task's expected outputs are rtl_source and testbench, and the formal gates apply only if a formal_spec file is produced, so none is submitted. The proof remains outstanding work against the spec's verification list."}], "files": [{"path": "axil_timer.v", "kind": "rtl_source", "title": "axil_timer: AXI4-Lite down-counting timer with interrupt", "summary": "Synthesizable Verilog-2001 implementation of [artifact:prj-97dea43f5b.interface-spec.a1] following [artifact:prj-97dea43f5b.microarchitecture.a1]. It has a synchronous active-low reset on every state flop, a latch-free combinational next-state block with defaults, and irq = expired && ie.", "entry": "axil_timer"}, {"path": "axil_timer_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "axil_timer self-checking testbench, lanes at ADDR_WIDTH 4 and 8", "summary": "Directed, self-checking testbench for the checks listed in section 8 of [artifact:prj-97dea43f5b.interface-spec.a1]. Every failure is reported with $error, passes are counted, and the NIRMAAN-SIM verdict is printed once before $finish. Counts are timed by edge counting, as the [artifact:prj-97dea43f5b.microarchitecture.a1] plan describes.", "entry": "axil_timer_tb"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["I have not linted, simulated or synthesized these files. The expected-value timings in the testbench come from reasoning about the RTL and spec by hand, not from a run.", "When EN is written 0 on a non-final edge, the count step still applies on that edge, as section 2 of the microarchitecture orders it. The testbench therefore expects COUNT = LOAD - (stop_edge - start_edge).", "The testbench uses $error, which needs SystemVerilog mode in Icarus (for example -g2012), and timing controls, which need --timing or --binary in Verilator."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Gaps this submission does not cover: no formal_spec (.sby) and no in-RTL `ifdef FORMAL` properties, so the spec's formal requirement and the design-intent assertions are still open. The testbench does not drive a read and a write on the same clock; the channels are independent in the RTL. The testbench has two parameterized lanes, axil_timer_tb_lane at ADDR_WIDTH 4 and 8, and the top axil_timer_tb adds up their pass and fail counts. All stimulus changes on negedges and DUT outputs are sampled at negedges."}
